 34   c  TITL$Nuclear Structure and Decay Data for A=34 Isobars                 
 34   c  AUTH$LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN                                            
 34   c  INST$Facility for Rare Isotope Beams, Michigan State University, East  
 34  2c  Lansing, MI 48824, USA                                                 
 34   c  ABST$This work presents a comprehensive and critical evaluation of     
 34  2c  experimental nuclear spectroscopic data from reactions and decays for  
 34  3c  all 11 nuclides with mass number 34 (Ne, Na, Mg, Al, Si, P, S, Cl, Ar, 
 34  4c  K, Ca). Recommended values are produced for level energies, spins and  
 34  5c  parities, half-lives, and radiation properties including energies,     
 34  6c  branching ratios, and multipolarities of |g rays, as well as           
 34  7c  characteristics of |b decay, based on a rigorous assessment of all     
 34  8c  available experimental data. Discrepancies among existing results are  
 34  9c  carefully addressed. This work supersedes earlier full evaluations of  
 34  Ac  A=34 published by 2012Ni10, 1990En08 (also 1998En04 update), and       
 34  Bc  1978En02.
 34   c  {+34}Cl and {+34}S remain the most extensively studied c  nuclides,    
 34  2c  investigated through more than 20 different reactions and c  decays,   
 34  3c  followed by {+34}P, {+34}Si, and {+34}Ar. {+34}Ne has been identified, 
 34  4c  but no nuclear structure information is available. Experimental plans  
 34  5c  to study the nuclear structure of {+34}Ne have been proposed at RIBF,  
 34  6c  RIKEN. For {+34}Na, no excited states have been confirmed and no |g    
 34  7c  rays have been placed with certainty. No |b{+-}-decay dataset exists   
 34  8c  for {+34}Na|){+34}Mg. {+34}Ca has not been identified, and an          
 34  9c  experiment has been conducted at FRIB in 2026 to identify {+34}Ca      
 34  Ac  through {+32}Ar+2p.                                                    
 34   c  CUT$Literature available up to September 30, 2026 has been consulted,  
 34  2c  with the help of the primary bibliographic source, the NSR database    
 34  3c  (2014Pr09) available at the Brookhaven National Laboratory web page:   
 34  4c  www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr/                                                  
 34   c  COMM$The statistical analysis of |g-ray data and deduced level schemes 
 34  2c  is carried out through a suite of current versions of computer codes,  
 34  3c  such as EvaluationToolkit, GLSC, Java-RULER, and ConsistencyCheck,     
 34  4c  available at the IAEA-NDS ENSDF codes web page                         
 34  5c  (https://www-nds.iaea.org/public/ensdf_pgm). The direct feedings to    
 34  6c  excited states in |b{+-} and |e decays have generally been computed    
 34  7c  from I(|g+ce) intensity balances at each level; the associated log     
 34  8c  {Ift} values are calculated using the BetaShape code. Theoretical total
 34  9c  conversion coefficients are calculated using version 2.3e of the BrIcc 
 34  Ac  code (2008Ki07) for the frozen-orbit option with an implicit           
 34  Bc  uncertainty of 1.4% when not stated. Q values and particle separation  
 34  Cc  energies have been adopted from 2021Wa16 (AME2020). Static magnetic    
 34  Dc  dipole moments are taken from 2019StZV (long-lived states) and 2020StZV
 34  Ec  (short-lived states) evaluations, and static electric quadrupole       
 34  Fc  moments from 2021StZZ evaluation, when available in these publications.
 34  Gc  Nuclear rms charge radii have been adopted from 2013An02 evaluation. In
 34  Hc  cases where weighted averaging has been used, the assigned uncertainty 
 34  Ic  in the result is generally at least as large as the smallest           
 34  Jc  uncertainty among the contributing data points. The evaluation workflow
 34  Kc  is aided by 'ENSDF-Agent'. Adopted levels are placed with the          
 34  Lc  assistance of the machine-learning tool 'Level-Matcher'.               
 34   c  ACKN$Earlier evaluations (2012Ni10, 1998En04 update, 1990En08,         
 34  2c  1978En02, 1973EnVA, 1967En05, 1962En05, 1957En01, 1954En19) and        
